From 2dfaa8498e8302e5c6d91bb9365465d26cc13840 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:01:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Share one Boltzmann constant between data and model, and
 check it per batch

equicdft.units defines DEFAULT_BOLTZMANN_CONSTANT (8.617333262e-5 eV/K);
GridData keeps using it and GridCACEModel now defaults to it as well
instead of 1.0. On every forward pass the model compares the batch's beta
with 1/(k_B T) under its own constant and raises a ValueError naming both
constants when they disagree, which used to pass silently and only mattered
for MetalWall and physical-mode models. Saved models are unaffected (they
record their constant); fresh reduced-unit models pass
boltzmann_constant=1.0 explicitly, as the tests, fixtures and the LJ
example now do. Golden outputs unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CKJKJnMQ5g5crBBPsN5iZn
