From b9eb30978d4ce5ea3068ce81c4b754cfcefde1d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:12:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Name the dimensionless chemical-potential outputs
 beta_mu_* with aliases

Model outputs are now beta_mu_local, beta_mu_average and beta_mu_weights,
matching the beta_ prefix of beta_F_exc, beta_mu and c1_plus_beta_mu; the
solver reports the equilibrium value as beta_mu in every path instead of
equilibrium_chemical_potential in some and both in others. Model outputs
and solver results are AliasedOutputs dictionaries: the old keys remain as
aliases of the same tensors and warn with EquicdftDeprecationWarning when
read through [] or .get (membership and iteration stay silent), until
0.2.0. Tests, the LJ example, README and DEPRECATIONS.md use the canonical
names; the goldens record canonical keys only (values unchanged).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CKJKJnMQ5g5crBBPsN5iZn
