From 0d6416d2dacaded6189309993595c18cb0a9364b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:24:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Make constructor options keyword-only, keeping the 0.0.x
 positional form for one release

Every public constructor now takes only its structural arguments
positionally (n_types for the local readouts, cutoff_grid and n_types for
PairwiseReadout, the wall geometry for MetalWall, max_power and
mean_density for the features, the three module inputs for GridCACEModel,
name/prediction/target for TensorLoss, ...) and the options by keyword;
GGAReadout lists n_types first like the other readouts. The keyword_only
decorator in equicdft._deprecation maps further positional arguments onto
the old parameter order with an EquicdftDeprecationWarning, so existing
calls keep binding correctly until 0.2.0, when they raise TypeError.
Configurations are keyword-based and unaffected. Golden outputs unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CKJKJnMQ5g5crBBPsN5iZn
